Linux also takes care of processors. So&nbsp;
if you're running two things in parallel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:59.440 --> 01:12:03.120
Linux will make sure that the right amount&nbsp;
of processors are dedicated to both.

01:12:04.400 --> 01:12:09.840
If you're, if you've ever run very computationally&nbsp;
intensive tasks on a laptop, you might notice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:09.840 --> 01:12:13.280
your browser gets laggy. That's because&nbsp;
it's not getting enough processor time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:16.880
So if you're running production&nbsp;
workloads, Linux needs to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:16.880 --> 01:12:21.840
that every program is getting its fair share&nbsp;
of processor time to run the actual program.

01:12:22.880 --> 01:12:30.800
Because disk, so Linux takes the files of all&nbsp;
